1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Listen to a talk in a history class.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:09,100
If you think about it, thanks to e-mail and computers we hardly write letters on paper anymore.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,741
Most people don’t even pay bills through the mail anymore,

4
00:00:12,741 --> 00:00:16,100
or mail informs to schools or to the government.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,000
It seems almost everything can be done online now.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,489
Keep in mind though that e-mail is a very recent development,

7
00:00:23,489 --> 00:00:28,220
but postal services systems for delivering physical paper letters and documents

8
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:32,210
and other items, well, they have been around for a long time.

9
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:39,160
For example, we know that in ancient times, documents were transported by riders on horseback.

10
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,729
They usually used a relay system,

11
00:00:41,729 --> 00:00:46,023
which means that one mail carrier would travel a certain distance with the mail

12
00:00:46,023 --> 00:00:49,856
and then pass it on to someone else, whose job was to take it

13
00:00:49,856 --> 00:00:51,080
the next part of the way.

14
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:56,420
In ancient China, for example, the government set up a large network of stations,

15
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:59,030
where fresh horses were kept.

16
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:05,110
So mail carriers could deliver official documents to far away parts of the kingdom more quickly.

17
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:12,369
Now during the Roman Empire, almost two thousand years ago, Roman rulers established their own system of roads

18
00:01:12,369 --> 00:01:16,300
and stations for mail delivery across the Empire’s vast lands.

19
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:22,554
Interestingly, even after the Roman Empire ended, its postal system remained intact;

20
00:01:22,554 --> 00:01:26,884
in other words, even though there was no official Roman Empire to govern the

21
00:01:26,884 --> 00:01:31,855
territories, the people living in the area found the postal system created by the Empire

22
00:01:31,855 --> 00:01:34,000
so useful that they continued to use it.

23
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:40,961
Then about five hundred years ago, during the Renaissance in Europe, different countries began to travel farther

24
00:01:40,961 --> 00:01:41,803
and farther,

25
00:01:41,803 --> 00:01:44,010
when they started trading goods.

26
00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:49,120
This led to a need for commercial documents to be delivered quickly and safely.

27
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:54,160
That’s when private business got involved and started their own postal systems.

28
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:58,940
So now it wasn’t only government that were delivering mail,

29
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:01,190
and that’s pretty much what it is like in the world today.

30
00:02:01,190 --> 00:02:04,802
Most governments operate their own postal services,

31
00:02:04,802 --> 00:02:10,039
but there are also many private companies that deliver letters and documents.

32
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:15,130
Of course, with today’s technology, there may soon be no need for any of them.
